    <Fragment slot='caption'>
      Thirteen years, one direction. The client era built machinery for surviving in the browser;
      everything since December 2020 has been about no longer needing to. Note what never shipped: a
      better fetch-in-effect, a nicer loading flag, a faster global store. The problems of the
      client era weren't refined; they were obsoleted. Dates are the official announcements
      (react.dev, nextjs.org, vercel.com).
    </Fragment>
